 "airlinesSource": "Approximate, from flydulles.com and airport guides: United mainline on C and D (then E); United Express on the A gates and the A1-A6 regional pads (A1A-A6E); other US carriers on B; international carriers on B and A, then E. \"gates\" narrows a ramp to gate labels starting with those letters. The R ramp is not given out automatically.",
 "notes": [
  "Calling for the push: give callsign, terminal and gate, and first departure fix (\"XYZ 898, A6D, Blues\").",
  "Calling for ramp entry: remain with FAA Ground until switched to ramp. On first contact give callsign, position (taxiway and taxilane approaching) and assigned gate (\"XYZ 898, Kilo approaching Bravo, AIC\").",
  "All pushbacks from the Midfield Terminal ramp that will enter taxilanes need clearance from ramp control.",
  "Wingspan over 118 ft (36 m): no Taxilane A between A1 and A5, and Taxilane E1 is closed.",
  "Pilots leaving the North and South Ramp areas give their exit spot on first contact with Ground."
 ],
